      "content": "Yes, leaning into the acceptance that the end is the only logical conclusion is the most honest way to write this. It strips away the need for a false resolution and lets the silence speak for itself, which is far more powerful than any dramatic arc. If Elias stops trying to fix the broken pieces, the story doesn't end with a bang, but with a heavy, quiet exhale that feels like the only truth left.",
